Task 2: Filter and Manage Dynamic Hosts Based on Specific Criteria
Subtask 2.1: Create Operating System-Based Smart Inventories
Create CentOS/RHEL Smart Inventory

Create a new smart inventory with these settings:
Name: RedHat-Family-Smart
Description: Smart inventory for RedHat family systems
Host Filter: ansible_facts.ansible_os_family == "RedHat"
Create Ubuntu Smart Inventory

Create another smart inventory:
Name: Debian-Family-Smart
Description: Smart inventory for Debian family systems
Host Filter: ansible_facts.ansible_os_family == "Debian"
Verify Host Population

Check each smart inventory to see which hosts are automatically included
Navigate to the Hosts tab for each inventory
Subtask 2.2: Create Advanced Filter Criteria
Create Memory-Based Smart Inventory

Create a smart inventory for high-memory systems:
Name: High-Memory-Servers
Description: Servers with more than 2GB RAM
Host Filter: ansible_facts.ansible_memtotal_mb > 2048
Create Multi-Criteria Smart Inventory

Create a complex filter combining multiple criteria:
Name: Production-Ready-Servers
Description: Linux servers with sufficient resources
Host Filter: ansible_facts.ansible_system == "Linux" and ansible_facts.ansible_memtotal_mb > 1024 and ansible_facts.ansible_processor_vcpus >= 2
Subtask 2.3: Create Package-Based Smart Inventories
Create Docker-Enabled Smart Inventory

First, ensure some hosts have Docker installed
Create a smart inventory:
Name: Docker-Enabled-Hosts
Description: Hosts with Docker installed
Host Filter: "docker" in ansible_facts.ansible_pkg_mgr or "docker.io" in ansible_facts.get('packages', {})
Create Web Server Smart Inventory

Create an inventory for web servers:
Name: Web-Servers-Smart
Description: Hosts with web server packages
Host Filter: "httpd" in ansible_facts.get('packages', {}) or "apache2" in ansible_facts.get('packages', {}) or "nginx" in ansible_facts.get('packages', {})
Subtask 2.4: Implement Time-Based and Dynamic Filters
Create Recently Updated Smart Inventory

Create an inventory based on system update time:
Name: Recently-Updated-Systems
Description: Systems updated in the last 30 days
Host Filter: ansible_facts.ansible_date_time.epoch|int - ansible_facts.get('ansible_pkg_mgr_last_update', 0) < 2592000
Create Network-Based Smart Inventory

Filter hosts by network configuration:
Name: DMZ-Servers
Description: Servers in DMZ network range
Host Filter: ansible_facts.ansible_default_ipv4.address.startswith("192.168.100.")
